From: truwa <oztruwa@gmail.com>
Subject: kosmickrisp: advertise depthBounds and fillModeNonSolid for idTech

idTech (DOOM 2016) and idTech 6.5 (Wolfenstein II) enable these at
vkCreateDevice without querying. Upstream 26.2.4 leaves them false, so
CreateDevice returns VK_ERROR_FEATURE_NOT_PRESENT on M1-M4.

Advertise the bits only. Do not call Metal setDepthTestMinBound; wiring
that on M5 made Wolf II world lighting worse.

---
 src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_physical_device.c | 16 +++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_physical_device.c b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_physical_device.c
index 0000000..1111111 100644
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_physical_device.c
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_physical_device.c
@@ -208,8 +208,22 @@ kk_get_device_features(
    *features = (struct vk_features){
       /* Vulkan 1.0 */
       .alphaToOne = true,
       .depthBiasClamp = true,
+      /* Metal 4 exposes native depth bounds on Apple GPU family 10+ (M5).
+       * idTech still enables the feature without querying it, so
+       * vkCreateDevice fails with VK_ERROR_FEATURE_NOT_PRESENT on M1-M4.
+       * Advertise it on every family; do not wire the Metal test — Wolf II
+       * lighting got worse when setDepthTestMinBound was actually applied.
+       */
+      .depthBounds = true,
       .depthClamp = true,
       .drawIndirectFirstInstance = true,
       .dualSrcBlend = true,
-      .fillModeNonSolid = false,
+      /* idTech 6.5 (Wolfenstein II) enables wireframe without querying. */
+      .fillModeNonSolid = true,
       .fragmentStoresAndAtomics = true,
       .fullDrawIndexUint32 = true,
       .imageCubeArray = true,
